/*!
\page usdProfiles_page_front UsdProfiles : USD Profile API Schema
\if ( PXRUSDAPI_DOXYGEN_BUILD )
\addtogroup usdProfiles
\endif

\section usdProfiles_overview Overview

UsdProfiles provides the \ref UsdProfilesProfileAPI "ProfileAPI" applied schema
for declaring that a prim (and its descendants) conform to a specific USD Profile.

A \em Profile is a named node in a capability DAG (directed acyclic graph)
representing a coherent set of functionality. Applying ProfileAPI to a prim
declares that the subtree rooted at that prim satisfies the capabilities
required by the named profile.

\section usdProfiles_resolution Profile Resolution

If no ProfileAPI is authored on a prim, the nearest ancestor's ProfileAPI
applies. Capability requirements do not propagate upward.

\section usdProfiles_registry Capability Registry

The \ref UsdProfilesCapabilityRegistry "CapabilityRegistry" is a singleton
that collects capability declarations from all loaded plugins' plugInfo.json
files. Capabilities are declared in a "Capabilities" section:

\code{.json}
{
    "Plugins": [{
        "Info": {
            "Capabilities": {
                "com.example.myCapability": {
                    "docstring": "My capability description",
                    "predecessors": ["usd"]
                }
            }
        }
    }]
}
\endcode

\section usdProfiles_profiles Profile Registry

The \ref UsdProfilesProfileRegistry "ProfileRegistry" resolves profiles
(capabilities with \c "isProfile": true) to their full transitive capability sets.

\section usdProfiles_usage Usage Example

\code{.py}
from pxr import Usd, UsdProfiles

stage = Usd.Stage.CreateInMemory()
root = stage.DefinePrim("/Robot", "Xform")

# Apply the ProfileAPI and set a profile
api = UsdProfiles.ProfileAPI.Apply(root)
api.GetProfileAttr().Set("com.nvidia.simready.prop_robotics_neutral")

# Query the effective profile
profile = UsdProfiles.GetEffectiveProfile(root)

# Check what capabilities the profile expands to
registry = UsdProfiles.CapabilityRegistry.GetInstance()
caps = registry.GetTransitivePredecessors(
    "com.nvidia.simready.prop_robotics_neutral")
\endcode

*/
